    "textSample": "< Skin Note THE CLAIM “Niacinamide and vitamin C cancel each other out.” Refuted myth Safe to combine WHY The myth traces to decades-old studies on raw, unformulated ingredients at high heat. In modern formulas the two are widely used together and can support a brighter-looking, more even complexion. Evidence grade Refuted · broad consensus Reviewed by a board-certified dermatologist. Source: Peer-reviewed formulation literature. ✦ General cosmetic information. For the appearance of skin, not medical advice. ♥ This helped Share note",
